%I A400236 #27 Oct 10 2026 15:44:54
%S A400236 6,4,18,24,4,54,108,54,4,162,432,360,96,4,486,1620,1890,900,150,4,
%T A400236 1458,5832,8748,6048,1890,216,4,4374,20412,37422,34020,15876,3528,294,
%U A400236 4,13122,69984,151632,171072,106920,36288,6048,384,4
%N A400236 Triangle read by rows: T(n,k) is the number of perfect matchings of the 3 X 2n Klein bottle grid with exactly n + 2k horizontal dominoes, n >= 1, k = 0, 1, ..., n.
%C A400236 Row n has n+1 terms. The last term of each row is always 4, which counts the perfect matchings where all dominoes are horizontal. This constant value reflects a structural constraint imposed by the Klein bottle topology.
%C A400236 The row polynomials F_n(q) = Sum_{k=0..n} T(n,k)*q^{n+2k} enumerate perfect matchings of the 3 X 2n Klein bottle grid weighted by the number of horizontal dominoes. By a parity invariant, every perfect matching M has h(M) == n (mod 2) horizontal dominoes, so F_n(q) contains only powers q^{n+2k}.
%C A400236 Row sums give A399564 (total number of perfect matchings of the 3 X 2n Klein bottle grid).
%D A400236 S.-M. Belcastro, Domino tilings of the Klein bottle, J. Combin. Theory Ser. A, 2023.
%D A400236 M. Bóna (ed.), Handbook of Enumerative Combinatorics, CRC Press / Chapman & Hall, 2015.
%H A400236 Jean Lauro Muller, <a href="/A400236/a400236.txt">Python program for computing the triangle</a>
%F A400236 F_n(q) = Sum_{M} q^{h(M)} = Sum_{k=0..n} T(n,k)*q^{n+2k}, where the first sum is over all perfect matchings M of the 3 X 2n Klein bottle grid, h(M) is the number of horizontal dominoes in M, and T(n,k) is the coefficient of q^{n+2k} in F_n(q).
%e A400236 Triangle begins:
%e A400236   n=1: 6, 4;
%e A400236   n=2: 18, 24, 4;
%e A400236   n=3: 54, 108, 54, 4;
%e A400236   n=4: 162, 432, 360, 96, 4;
%e A400236   n=5: 486, 1620, 1890, 900, 150, 4;
%e A400236   n=6: 1458, 5832, 8748, 6048, 1890, 216, 4.
%e A400236 For n=3, the row polynomial is F_3(q) = 54*q^3 + 108*q^5 + 54*q^7 + 4*q^9. The coefficients [54, 108, 54, 4] give row 3 of the triangle, and their sum is 54 + 108 + 54 + 4 = 220 = A399564(3).
%Y A400236 Row sums give A399564.
%Y A400236 Cf. A398567, A398672, A397309.
